<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Orontid dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century–c. 200 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> · Also known as Yervanduni dynasty, Eruandids</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Orontid dynasty ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> from the Achaemenid period until about 200 BCE. Its members governed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrapy</a> of Armenia for the Persian kings and were linked to the Persian royal house by marriage, then reigned as effectively independent kings after the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a>, from Armavir and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yervandashat">Yervandashat</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-iii-the-great">Antiochus III</a> ended their rule around 200 BCE, and Armenia passed to the Artaxiads.</p></div>
